by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-07T14:40:54Z

Thank you @cs278.

The original `min(\PHP_INT_MAX, ...)` did not clamp in the case you reported: the product rounds to exactly `(float) \PHP_INT_MAX`, the two arguments compare equal, and `min()` returns the float, so `testEffectivelyInfiniteBurstSize` stayed red. I amended the branch to cap at `2147483647` instead, which sidesteps that (the bound is exactly representable as a double), keeps the value in range on 32-bit platforms, and stays acceptable as a Redis TTL.

I also extended `RateTest` to cover the boundary case, turned `testEffectivelyInfiniteBurstSize` into a real assertion, and rebased on 6.4.

