by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-07T14:47:44Z

Also capped the burst size itself at `2147483647`. `TokenBucket::__serialize()` packs it into a 32-bit field, so anything larger wrapped on the first round trip through storage: the second `consume()` reported `4294967294` remaining instead of decrementing. Capping in `TokenBucket` and `TokenBucketLimiter` keeps the reported limit and the stored one in agreement.
